    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Humidity is categorized into Absolute, Relative, and Specific Humidity, with Relative Humidity measured as a percentage of moisture saturation.",
        "Clouds are categorized based on height into High, Middle, Low, and Vertical development clouds.",
        "Rainfall occurs in three main types: Convectional, Orographic (relief-induced), and Cyclonic (frontal) rainfall.",
        "Condensation leads to various precipitation and atmospheric phenomena including dew, frost, fog, mist, and clouds."
